        "content": "<p>qiyuhuating opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14981\">PR #14981</a> from <code>qiyuhuating:fix/aarch64-stack-limit-chain-offset-14946</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #14946.</p>\n<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>When loading a nested stack_limit global value on AArch64, x16 may hold the base of the next load. Materializing a large offset into x16 destroys that base and yields a bad address or a crash.</p>\n<h2>Change</h2>\n<p>Use the reserved x17 temporary for offset materialization when the base register is x16; otherwise retain x16.</p>\n<h2>Regression coverage</h2>\n<p>Add a Cranelift .clif run test for nested stack-limit loads with large negative offsets, covering AArch64 and x86_64.</p>\n<h2>Validation</h2>\n<p>Not compiled or run locally. Please validate with Cranelift filetests and AArch64 CI before marking ready.</p>\n</blockquote>",
